        targets a particular person;
      </li>
      <li>
        use a published page as a way to advertise, to host files, or to reach an audience for
        something that is not a tabletop encounter.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Deciding what breaks this is ours to do, and we do it case by case. Where something is
      borderline we would rather ask you than remove it, and where it is not we remove it.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your content</h2>
    <p>
      You keep ownership of the content you create — custom creatures, spells, campaigns,
